  "lead": "Fall enrollment in degree-granting postsecondary institutions was <b>18,580,026</b> in 2022 (SRC-608-01). Massachusetts enrolled <b>468,960</b>, rank 12 of 51 (derived, SRC-608-01). The SAT mean total score for 2023 graduates was <b>1028</b> in the United States, with 51.2% of graduates taking the test (SRC-608-02). Massachusetts scored <b>1112</b> (57.0% taking the test) (SRC-608-02). Degree-granting institutions employed <b>1,530,513</b> faculty in Fall 2023 (SRC-608-03). State faculty counts are not in that national table. The IPEDS 6-year bachelor's graduation rate for the 2017 entry cohort was <b>64.5%</b> at all 4-year institutions (SRC-608-04). That Digest table is national; it has no state column. A state-level faculty table is not in the current Digest xlsx set. Full-time faculty numbered <b>859,825</b> in Fall 2023; <b>192,300</b> were professors and <b>48.8%</b> were women (SRC-608-05). That Digest table is national and has no state column.",
